          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best whey protein powder is the one that gives you clean, honestly labeled protein at a cost per 25 g you can sustain every day. For most people that is an isolate-led blend like Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard. If budget rules, Myprotein Impact Whey is the value play. If lactose or macros give you a real reason to spend more, Dymatize ISO100 is the isolate to buy, Naked Whey covers grass-fed and single-ingredient buyers, Platinum Hydrowhey is the fallback for sensitive stomachs, and Ghost Whey is the pick when flavor keeps you consistent.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, judge it on protein per scoop, the order of its ingredients, its certification status and its cost per 25 g of protein. Then focus on what actually builds muscle: hard training and enough total protein every day. Work out your number with the <a href="/protein-calculator/">protein calculator</a>, and compare across categories in our <a href="/best-protein-powder/">best protein powder</a> rankings.
